set heading(numbering: none)

`square` · enclose · a boxed version with equal sides.

# Form

`x.square` on a symbol, `(a + b).square` on a group. A recipe has one base and up to three operations.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `x.square` | $x.square$ | built and cached |
| `F.bb.square` | $F.bb.square$ | built and cached |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | A boxed version with equal sides. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | Use a `sym` to give a recipe a short name. |
| Construction | A shape around the base: a circle, a box or a square. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- More than three operations on one base gives a warning.
- `square` is also a named symbol, the empty square. After a dot it is the operation.

# From LaTeX

no LaTeX command.

